    "knowledge_point": "Comparing a Polynomial Function and a Logarithmic Function",
    "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}.$",
    "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since $x≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ for large values of $x,$ the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}=0.\n$$",
