    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers are mathematically correct and explicitly supported by their respective captured worked solutions. Conjugation reverses the imaginary part and fixes real numbers; z plus its conjugate equals twice its real part, and their product equals the squared modulus. The right Riemann sum gives 5(25+27+k+18)=450, hence k=20. At x=3, f(3) is undefined; both one-sided limits are negative infinity, so unequal one-sided limits are not the reason. Exponentials dominate powers and logarithms, while positive powers dominate logarithms, giving the stated limits. The bounded sine numerator divided by a denominator growing in magnitude tends to zero. The logarithmic asymptote occurs where 4-2x=0. Completing the square gives 4(w-5)^2=25 and w=5±5/2. Source notation and the selected choices express the same answers. No prior submitted answer or captured grade was supplied.",
